Z||000000||fropuff||11-20-2000||09:48 PM||||Hey, I just got an antenna kit for my 80 Cutlass to go to the new AM/FM.  I was wondering how I can hook it up.  I have an existing antenna, the one in the windshield.  How can I hook it up?  It just says to plug it into the radio.  It also says that I should adjust the trimmer to get better reception.  Can anyone help me out?  Thanks a lot.  I kind of want to start tomorrow if I can, so I kind of need to know if I can use it.  Thanks again.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||11-21-2000||12:13 AM||||I think the hardest part is running the antenna lead. I had an 87 Ciera that I put a new antenna on. I wound up drilling through the trunklid and running it under the backseat, the doorsills and up under the dash. Sounds like a lot of work, but the clearances around the front fender made it difficult to put it up there. Plus, it gave it the undercover narc-mobile look, hehehe. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||11-21-2000||04:23 PM||||So it will work?  I'm putting it on the front right fender.  Then you just run it under and through the firewall, to the radio.  The only thing I need to know now is how to connect it.  How do I do this?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||11-21-2000||04:52 PM||||I just figured it out.  It can't be more straight-forward than what it is.  I'm going to start tomorrow after school.  I have to drill a hole in the fender first.  Then run the wire, plug it in, and it should work.  Thanks for the help anyway.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||11-21-2000||06:19 PM||||Okay, I'm a little impatient, so I started it tonight.  I got the antenna hooked to the FM, and it works GREAT!  I can pick up about 10 FM stations and NO AM stations.  That's really too bad.  Who listens to AM anyway?  I had it hanging out the side window, and it works real good.  I will mount it to the fender tomorrow.  It does work good though.  Best $33.00 I've spent.  $25 for the AM/FM, $8 for the antenna kit.  Now all I need is some 3.5s for the front dash, and some 4x10s that I have to wire up for the rear deck.  Then I should be set.  Then I need some snow tires, sand bags, right side door mirror, and that exhaust leak fixed.  Thanks for the help.  I just wanted to know if I could use it.  Thanks again. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||10
